# Always commit and deploy

After a completed, tested fix in this repo:

- Commit the relevant source and tests (never `.env` or secrets).
- Push `master` to `origin` (GitHub is what containers pull).
- Deploy so production picks it up. For `.py`/asset-only changes, push then recreate the postmortem container (`postmortem_stop.ps1` + `postmortem_start.ps1`) so start-time `git pull` runs. Rebuild with `deploy_postmortem.ps1` when requirements or the Dockerfile change.
